{%- comment -%}
  Cart trust row: a compact line of reassurance directly above the checkout
  button, in the cart drawer and on the cart page. It answers the last "what if"
  at the moment of paying, which is where it earns its place.

  Every item is true for the store it runs on; the theme never invents a promise:
  - Secure checkout: always (Shopify's checkout is encrypted and PCI compliant).
  - Free shipping over X: only when the merchant has set a free-shipping
    threshold, and read from that same setting, so it can never disagree with
    the progress bar. (Whether checkout honours it is the store's shipping
    configuration.) The sentence comes from snippets/free-shipping-claim, the
    one every other free-shipping mention in the theme uses too.
  - Returns: a link to the store's actual refund policy, and only when one
    exists. No "30-day returns" default.
  - Guarantee: the merchant's own words, only when they write some.
  At most three items show; the guarantee takes the returns slot when there is
  no refund policy.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.cart_show_trust -%}
  {%- capture shipping_claim -%}{% render 'free-shipping-claim' %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign show_shipping = false
    if shipping_claim != blank
      assign show_shipping = true
    endif
    assign refund_policy = shop.refund_policy
    assign guarantee = settings.cart_trust_guarantee | strip
    assign item_count = 1
    if show_shipping
      assign item_count = item_count | plus: 1
    endif
  -%}
  <ul class="cart-trust" role="list">
    <li class="cart-trust__item">
      {% render 'icon', name: 'lock' %}
      <span>{{ 'cart.trust.secure_checkout' | t }}</span>
    </li>
    {%- if show_shipping -%}
      <li class="cart-trust__item">
        {% render 'icon', name: 'truck' %}
        <span>{{ shipping_claim }}</span>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if refund_policy != blank -%}
      <li class="cart-trust__item">
        {% render 'icon', name: 'return' %}
        <a class="cart-trust__link" href="{{ refund_policy.url }}">{{ 'cart.trust.returns' | t }}</a>
      </li>
      {%- assign item_count = item_count | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if guarantee != blank and item_count < 3 -%}
      <li class="cart-trust__item">
        {% render 'icon', name: 'sparkle' %}
        <span>{{ guarantee | escape }}</span>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}
  </ul>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* One quiet line of fine print beside the taxes note: muted, the same caption
     size, icons in the trust-badge stroke style. It wraps rather than truncates,
     so a long guarantee or a German label never gets cut. */
  .cart-trust {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-5);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .cart-trust__item { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-2); min-height: 24px; }
  .cart-trust__item .icon { width: 1rem; height: 1rem; flex: none; }
  /* The returns link: underlined so it reads as a link, and padded to a 24px
     target without making the row taller. */
  .cart-trust__link {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    padding-block: 4px;
    transition: color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-editorial);
  }
  .cart-trust__link:hover { color: var(--color-text); }
{% endstylesheet %}
